      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Behavioral pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 2: know intent, structure, one example</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Template Method</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Write the recipe once in a base class, leave a few blanks, and let subclasses fill only the blanks. Learn abstract steps vs hooks, why the template method is <code>final</code>, the Hollywood principle, and the question every interviewer asks: Template Method or Strategy?</p>\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Before this page:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-oop-interfaces\">Interfaces</a> (program to an interface), <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-oop-polymorphism\">Polymorphism</a> (one call, many bodies), and <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-uml-class\">UML class diagrams</a> for the notation in the Structure picture (arrows and diamonds: <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-uml-relationships\">relationships</a>).</p>\n"
  },
